# #286: songs and books the player can't play stay in the library, drawn
# greyed with the can't-play glyph at the right edge (apps/ipodui/list.c).
# SELECT on such a row says why (owner, 2026-11-13; screens/noplay.c): a
# light page over the list, "Can't Play Song" / "Can't Play Audiobook",
# a heading and one sentence for the reason (protected, or format not
# supported), OK. Nothing plays, nothing stops, the queue is untouched;
# OK (SELECT) or MENU returns to the list on the same row and scroll
# (# same: the list before the press == the list after the page). The
# video kind (the "Can't Play Video" page) needs the sim with the player:
# ipodui-p14a-fallback. The reason comes
# from the parsers at scan time (TAGCACHE_UI_UNPLAYABLE() of the flag
# word); the lists read it from RAM. Fixtures (tests/fixtures/
# make_p090f1_fixtures.py), on a disk of their own:
#   Music/plain.m4a       "Plain", AAC: plays
#   Music/drm.m4p         "Plain", a protected store purchase (reason 1)
#   Music/ac3.m4a         "AC3", AC-3 in MP4: no decoder (reason 3)
#   Music/plain.mp3       "Plain Song": plays
#   Audiobooks/book.aax   "Plain", a protected audiobook (reason 2)
#   Audiobooks/book.aa    "Protected Book", Audible .aa (reason 2)
#   Audiobooks/type.m4b   "Classify Type Book": plays
#   Podcasts/ac3.m4a      "AC3" again, a podcast episode (the folder):
#                         no decoder (reason 3)
# The loose ends (2026-11-13, p090-286tail), each asserted below:
#   - Search draws a result that can't play greyed with the glyph, as
#     the library's lists (one helper: the list's unplayable callback on
#     lib_row_unplayable(); a book result reads its book's file):
#     "noplay row=... why=3" between ab_mark s0/s1 (the "ac" results),
#     "why=2" between b0/b1 (the "pro" results, Protected Book); SELECT
#     on the book result shows the page (kind=book), not the
#     book's own page; on the episode result "Can't Play Episode".
#   - On-The-Go draws its unplayable rows greyed (o0/o1: row 1, the
#     .m4p, why=1); SELECT on it shows the page ("otg list noplay
#     select row=1 why=1") and plays nothing (expect_stopped); SELECT on
#     a playable row plays from there, as before (expect_queue 2
#     /Music/plain.m4a).
#   - A podcast episode gets "Can't Play Episode" (kind=episode), in
#     Podcasts and in Search.
#   - The hold menu never offers Add to On-The-Go for a row that can't
#     play (the item is left out, as for a video; the menu has no greyed
#     items): the .m4p song items=76 (Browse Album, Browse Artist,
#     Cancel), the protected book and the episode items=64 (Cancel).
#     A playable album row keeps it (items=65) and adds both its songs.
#   - (p090-int3; orchestrator, 2026-11-13) a row that can't play shows
#     no blue "unplayed" dot: the never-played AC3 episode (podcast) and
#     its show, whose only episode it is (podcast_shows). The golden
#     regions cover the dot column only, every row (episodes x 0-16,
#     shows x 56-78). Red on the p090-int3 merge sim (library.c before
#     the fix): 76 dot pixels in each region.
# Red (the p090-286why sim, before these): no search/OTG "noplay row"
# lines between the marks, OTG SELECT plays (no "otg list noplay"),
# kind=song for the episode, items=77/65 on the greyed rows.
# The sim build has no video player (HAVE_BCMFW_VIDEO), so Videos is not
# shown; the album track list (Unknown Album) stands in for it.
# Red without the greying: no "noplay row" line (list.c's sim trace of a
# greyed row); without the SELECT guard (screens/browse.c) the press
# plays the list from that row and expect_stopped fails. Red (2026-11-13)
# with the guard back to "does nothing": no "noplay page" lines, the
# page shots equal the lists; with the page stopping the audio: the
# "audio=1" lines and expect_playing fail.
# The glyph's place (list.c's "noplay glyph" trace: its ink's top-left,
# 13 px square, in the row; owner 2026-11-13, option A, a little bigger
# and centred): right-aligned to x 313, where the chevron's ink ends;
# centred on the text, so y 14 in a 44 px song row (the two-line block,
# 6-34), y 20 in a 55 px book row (block 12-40) and y 6 in a 25 px track
# row (cap rows 7-17). Red: a 1 px move (y=15 in the song row) fails.
# The queue [playable, unplayable, playable] skips the middle entry:
# wait_index 3 reaches the third.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-286-unplayable.script
# disk: bare
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/f1/plain.m4a Music/plain.m4a
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/f1/drm.m4p Music/drm.m4p
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/f1/ac3.m4a Music/ac3.m4a
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/plain.mp3 Music/plain.mp3
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/f1/book.aax Audiobooks/book.aax
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/f1/book.aa Audiobooks/book.aa
# disk-file: tests/ui/fixtures/p146/type.m4b Audiobooks/type.m4b
# disk-file: tests/fixtures/f1/ac3.m4a Podcasts/ac3.m4a
# log: noplay row=
# log: why=1 sel=
# log: why=2 sel=
# log: why=3 sel=
# log: noplay glyph row=0 x=301 y=14 d=13 h=44
# log: noplay glyph row=1 x=301 y=20 d=13 h=55
# log: noplay glyph row=1 x=301 y=6 d=13 h=25
# log: noplay page why=3 kind=song audio=0
# log: noplay page why=1 kind=song audio=0
# log: noplay page why=2 kind=book audio=1
# log: noplay page why=1 kind=song audio=1
# log: noplay page dismiss key=menu audio=0
# log: noplay page dismiss key=select audio=0
# log: noplay page dismiss key=menu audio=1
# log: noplay page dismiss key=select audio=1
# expect-file: /.rockbox/ipodui.log list can't play why=2 kind=1
# log: expect_queue ok n=2
# log: expect_playing ok
# log: stats finish idx=0
# nolog: stats finish idx=1
# nolog: expect_playing failed
# nolog: expect_queue failed
# nolog: splash-suppressed
# same: songs songs_back
# same: songs_drm songs_drm_back
# same: books books_back
# same: album album_back
# same: search search_back
# log: search noplay select row=
# log: noplay page why=3 kind=song audio=1
# logbetween: s0 s1 noplay row=\d+ why=3 sel=
# logbetween: s0 s1 noplay page why=3 kind=episode
# logbetween: b0 b1 noplay row=\d+ why=2 sel=
# logbetween: b0 b1 noplay page why=2 kind=book
# logbetween: o0 o1 noplay row=1 why=1 sel=
# logbetween: o0 o1 otg list noplay select row=1 why=1
# logbetween: o0 o1 noplay page why=1 kind=song audio=0
# logbetween: p0 p1 noplay page why=3 kind=episode audio=0
# logbetween: p0 p1 hold open ctx=song items=64
# logbetween: h0 h1 hold open ctx=song items=76
# logbetween: h2 h3 hold open ctx=group items=64
# logbetween: h4 h5 hold open ctx=group items=65
# logbetween: h4 h5 hold act add rc=2
# log: expect_queue ok n=2 first=/Music/plain.m4a
# nolog: hold open ctx=song items=77
# nolog: otg list noplay select row=0
# same: otg_sel otg_back
# same: podcast podcast_back
# golden: skip songs songs_back song_format songs_drm songs_drm_back song_protected hold_song books books_back book_protected hold_book album album_back album_page search search_page search_back search_ep episode_search_page search_book search_book_page otg otg_sel otg_page otg_back episode_page podcast_back hold_episode
# golden-region: podcast_shows 56 20 79 240
# golden-region: podcast 0 20 17 240
# timeout: 300

wait 1000
wait_db 30000
repeat off
key SELECT          # Music
wait 800
wheel +3            # Songs
wait 300
key SELECT
wait 2000
shot songs          # AC3 selected (greyed, can't play), the rest below
expect_drawn AC3
expect_drawn Plain Song

# SELECT on the unplayable row: the page says why; nothing plays
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot song_format    # Can't Play Song: Format not supported
expect_stopped
key MENU            # back to Songs, AC3 still selected
wait 1200
shot songs_back
wheel +2            # the second "Plain": the protected purchase (.m4p)
wait 600
shot songs_drm
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot song_protected # Can't Play Song: Protected file
expect_stopped
key SELECT          # OK
wait 1200
shot songs_drm_back
ab_mark h0
hold SELECT 1500    # the hold menu on the .m4p: no Add to On-The-Go
wait 600
shot hold_song      # Browse Album / Browse Artist / Cancel
key MENU            # Cancel
wait 800
ab_mark h1
key MENU            # Music
wait 700

# Now with a song playing (two in the queue, the first on repeat one, so
# the playing track and its mark hold still): the pages leave it alone
repeat one
play_files /Music/plain.mp3 /Music/plain.m4a
wait 800
expect_playing 300
wheel +3            # Audiobooks (Songs + 3)
wait 300
key SELECT
wait 2000
wheel +1            # "Plain" (.aax): greyed
wait 600
shot books
expect_drawn Protected Book
expect_drawn Classify Type Book
key SELECT          # Can't Play Audiobook: Protected file
wait 1500
shot book_protected
expect_playing 500
expect_queue 2 /Music/plain.mp3
key MENU            # back to Audiobooks, "Plain" still selected
wait 1200
shot books_back
expect_playing 300
ab_mark h2
hold SELECT 1500    # the protected book: Cancel only
wait 600
shot hold_book
key MENU
wait 800
ab_mark h3
key MENU            # Music
wait 700

wheel -4            # Albums
wait 300
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +2            # Plain Artist's Unknown Album
wait 300
key SELECT          # its track list: Plain (plays), Plain (.m4p)
wait 2000
expect_drawn Plain
wheel +1            # the .m4p: greyed
wait 600
shot album
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot album_page     # Can't Play Song: Protected file, over the album
expect_playing 300
expect_queue 2 /Music/plain.mp3
key SELECT          # OK
wait 1200
shot album_back
expect_playing 300
key MENU            # Albums
wait 600
ab_mark h4
hold SELECT 1500    # Plain Artist's Unknown Album: it plays, so Add
wait 600
key SELECT          # Add to On-The-Go: Plain (.m4a), Plain (.m4p)
wait 800
ab_mark h5
key MENU            # Music, Albums selected
wait 600

# Search: a result that can't play gets the same page (search.c)
wheel +5 300        # Search (Albums + 5: no Compilations here)
wait 400
ab_mark s0
key SELECT
wait 800
type ac
wait 800
key MENU            # the strip hides: the first result selected
wait 800
shot search
expect_drawn AC3
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot search_page    # Can't Play Song: Format not supported
expect_playing 300
expect_queue 2 /Music/plain.mp3
key MENU
wait 1200
shot search_back
expect_playing 300
wheel +1 300        # the episode "AC3" (its podcast)
wait 600
shot search_ep
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot episode_search_page    # Can't Play Episode: Format not supported
expect_playing 300
key MENU
wait 1200
ab_mark s1
audio_stop
repeat off
wait 500
key MENU            # Music (the strip is hidden: MENU leaves Search)
wait 600

# Search again: a book result that can't play (Protected Book)
ab_mark b0
key SELECT          # Search
wait 800
type pro
wait 800
key MENU            # the strip hides: the first result selected
wait 800
shot search_book
expect_drawn Protected Book
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot search_book_page   # Can't Play Audiobook: Protected file
expect_stopped
key MENU
wait 1200
ab_mark b1
key MENU            # Music
wait 600

# On-The-Go: Plain (plays), Plain (.m4p, greyed)
wheel -7 300        # Playlists (Search - 7)
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
ab_mark o0
key SELECT          # On-The-Go
wait 1200
shot otg
wheel +1 300        # the .m4p
wait 600
shot otg_sel
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot otg_page       # Can't Play Song: Protected file
expect_stopped
key MENU
wait 1200
shot otg_back
ab_mark o1
wheel -1 300        # Plain (.m4a): plays On-The-Go from there
wait 600
key SELECT
wait 1500
expect_playing 300
expect_queue 2 /Music/plain.m4a
audio_stop
wait 500
key MENU            # Now Playing -> On-The-Go
wait 800
key MENU            # Playlists
wait 600
key MENU            # Music
wait 600
key MENU            # main menu
wait 600

# Podcasts: the episode that can't play
wheel +1 300        # Podcasts
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
shot podcast_shows  # the show: no unplayed dot (its one episode can't play)
key SELECT          # the show (Unknown Album)
wait 1200
ab_mark p0
shot podcast
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot episode_page   # Can't Play Episode: Format not supported
expect_stopped
key MENU
wait 1200
shot podcast_back
hold SELECT 1500    # an episode that can't play: Cancel only
wait 600
shot hold_episode
key MENU
wait 800
ab_mark p1
key MENU            # Podcasts
wait 600
key MENU            # main menu
wait 600

# The queue: playable, unplayable, playable
play_files /Music/plain.mp3 /Music/drm.m4p /Music/plain.m4a
wait 500
expect_playing 500
wait_index 3 30000  # the third (plain.m4a, ~1 s) after the first
quit
